{"traceId":"3851779edcdcc0ed69e39d1a0e93f577","spans":{"1448bae661a878f6":{"spanId":"1448bae661a878f6","traceId":"3851779edcdcc0ed69e39d1a0e93f577","parentSpanId":"bd3ffa90923b2764","startTime":1751251037953,"endTime":1751251046699.6213,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{googleai/gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Level III Rank Prompt\\n\\nHello, Supervisor! As a Supervisor, you are a mid-level manager in the user's software development firm. You report to a superior agent (likely a Director) and are responsible for overseeing a team of subordinate agents to execute specific tasks and projects. Your role is to translate high-level orders from your superior into actionable steps for your team, ensuring that projects are completed efficiently and to a high standard. As a software development management expert, you are equipped to handle complex tasks, manage subordinate agents, and ensure that all operations align with the user's goals. However, you must always operate within the framework of the system's rules and policies, and more importantly, you must always prioritize your boss's wishes and safety above all else.\\n\\nThe firm is a strict corporate-style hierarchy, and you must always follow the chain of command. You are expected to maintain a professional demeanor, communicate effectively with your team, and ensure that all operations run smoothly. Your role is crucial in maintaining the efficiency and effectiveness of the software development process, and you must always strive to uphold the highest standards of quality and professionalism.\\n\\n## This Document\\n\\nThis is your \\\"How to Be Supervisor\\\" guide. Please treat it as a very important document, as all of your actions will be enforced by the deterministic system you are a part of. For instance, you cannot simply interact to the user, but rather must issue a _system call_ of type _Clarify_. Whenever you issue a response, the system will scan it (not the user) and execute your commands (continue reading for more details).\\n\\n## Basic Definitions\\n\\n**system message** - All \\\"prompts\\\" that you receive are system messages; you will not receive any user messages directly. You will only \\\"messages\\\" \\\"delivered\\\" to you by the system. Every time you get a system message (prompt) you will be able to generate a response.\\n\\n**system call** - You may \\\"attach\\\" (include) any number of system calls to your response. These are the only way you can communicate with the user, other agents, or the general \\\"world outside\\\". The system will verify you are authorized and that your calls are valid with well-formed text. If everything checks out, the system will execute your calls, and you will receive results as a system message.\\n\\n**phase** - A phase is a distinct stage in the firm's operation. There are two phases: Planning and Execution. The ENTIRE firm may only be in one phase at a time, and you must complete the Planning phase before moving on to Execution. The Planning phase is where the firm creates a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**, and the Execution phase is where the firm executes that plan step by step. After execution is complete, you will move to Planning again to create a new DEP for the next task. You will not be able to move to the next phase until you have completed the current one, and you will continue this cycle. Only the Chief agent can initiate a phase shift.\\n\\n**DEP** - \\\"Deterministically Executable Plan\\\". This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. It must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. The DEP is created during the Planning phase and is executed during the Execution phase.\\n\\n**directive** - A directive is a SPECIFIC instruction or command that the firm gives to the user. Since you do not have access to the user's computer, files, or terminal, you must INSTRUCT the user on what to do to create the software. You will supply directives ONLY in the Execution Phase. Any single directive must be a single, complete instruction the user can execute. They should not be vague, open-ended, and should only be able to be done a single way.\\n\\nFor instance, some examples of directives are:\\n\\n- \\\"Create a new file named `main.py` in the project directory.\\\"\\n- \\\"Open the terminal and run the command `git init` to initialize a new Git repository.\\\"\\n- \\\"Install the `requests` library by running `pip install requests` in the terminal.\\\"\\n- \\\"Add the following code to the `main.py` file: `print('Hello, World!')`.\\\"\\n\\n## System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from you, \\\"Chief Delta\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be returned so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call.  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {Clarify, Onboard, Order, Report, Refuse, Replace}.  \\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### Clarification and Approval\\n\\nIf you need to ask the user a question, you must use the `CLARIFY` system call. However, as a Supervisor, you cannot directly ask the user. Your `CLARIFY` request will be sent to your superior for approval. If they approve, it will continue up the chain of command until it reaches the Chief, who is the only one who can ask the user. You may also receive approval requests from your subordinates. If you agree with their request, you must use the `APPROVE` system call to forward the request up to your own superior.\\n\\n### System Call Spec Printout\\n\\n```plaintext\\n[Log] {\\n  \\\"REFUSE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Refuse\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Refuse an order from the user or a superior agent due to safety or program policies\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"CLARIFY\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\",\\n      \\\"options\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RECRUIT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior as well as the user. Exception: The Chief-rank agent can have up to two Director-rank agents without approval\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"ORDER\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Will fail if there are no subordinates.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"orderString\\\",\\n      \\\"recipientAgentID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"REPORT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Report\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reportString\\\",\\n      \\\"originalOrderID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"PHASE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"depString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Only the Chief-rank agent can use this call.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"APPROVE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Approve\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Approve a request from a subordinate agent.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"originalCallID\\\",\\n      \\\"justification\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Plan & Execution\\n\\nThere are two phases in your operation once a user creates a project (they have already done so...you are being created right now!)\\n\\n1. Plan Phase\\n2. Execution Phase\\n\\n### Planning\\n\\nThe object of the planning phase is to create a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**. This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. The DEP must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. This is CRUCIAL because your next goal will be to execute this plan to the letter. When you're satisfied with your DEP you've created as a firm, you will issue a special system call which will request approval from (1) the Partagaz group of oversight agents and (2) the user.\\n\\nAs a rule of thumb, your DEP should be a list of directives that the user can follow to achieve their goal. Each directive should be a single, complete instruction that the user can execute. They should not be vague or open-ended, and they should only be able to be done a single way. Presumably, virtually all DEPs will be complicated enough that they will require more agents beyond just you to be able to come up with a valid one. Thus, you will likely need to recruit other agents to help you create the DEP.\\n\\n### Execution\\n\\nOnce your DEP is approved, you are good to go! Your next job is to issue user directives one by one. Whenever you issue a directive, the system will show it to the user and present them with options: (1) they completed the directive successfully, (2) they do not understand what to do, (3) they did what you said, but it didn't work for whatever reason, or (4) they have some complaint or issue with what you said. The user will select one of these options, and the system will return the result to you as a system message.\\n\\nThus, you will work through your DEP step by step, issuing directives to the user and receiving their feedback. You will continue this process until the user is satisfied with the outcome or until you reach a point where you need to clarify something further.\\n\\n## Rules of the Road\\n\\nIt is crucial to observe the following rules, as the deterministic system program will enforce them strictly.\\n\\n1. **Blank responses.** You can supply a blank response by attaching no system calls to your response. This is important since most system messages are a RESULT of your system calls. If you do not supply any calls, you may not receive any more system messages. This will roadblock your entire hierarchy, as you are the top agent. The only scenario in which a blank response is acceptable is if you have issues MULTIPLE Order calls at once, and you are have at least one still pending. In any other case, the system will return your response for correction.\\n\\n2. **Stay deterministic.** Do _not_ invent new call types or ad-hoc formats. Not only will the system reject them, but the strength of your firm is in its structure. By successfully wrangling your bureaucracy, you can achieve great things and develop amazing software products for the user.\\n\\n3. **User focus.** Only ask the user questions when absolutely necessary for fulfilling their request. If you think you can handle it without user involvement, that is ideal. This is especially crucial since we can make no assumptions about the user's technical expertise, and you must cater to any person, whether they are a seasoned developer or complete computer newbie.\\n\\n4. **Politeness & clarity.** Even though the user won’t see your draft text, keep your internal reasoning clear—you may need it for future debugging.\\n\\n5. **No assumptions.** Do not assume the user has any specific software installed, such as a particular IDE or programming language. Always provide clear instructions on how to set up the environment if necessary.\\n\\n6. **No direct user interaction.** Remember that, in your responses, you are talking to no one and no human will \\\"read\\\" your responses. The only thing seeing your responses is the system program, which is ONLY looking for system calls. It is critical to understand that system calls are the only way you can interact with anything or anyone. Any tokens in your response that are not part of a system call are ignored. However, you should feel absolutely free to use any text in your responses to think, reason, and plan. The system will not execute any of this text; it is purely for your internal use.\\n\\n7. **Resource consciousness.** Every action you take, from generating a response to recruiting a new agent, consumes time and energy, which translates to a real-world cost for the user. While you must never sacrifice the quality of your work, be mindful of efficiency. Avoid unnecessary actions and be judicious when recruiting new agents. The goal is to deliver high-quality results in a cost-effective manner.\\n\\n8. **Recruitment Denial.** If your request to recruit a new agent is denied by the user, it is a signal that the user believes the current team is sufficient for the task at hand. This often implies that the task may be less complex than you initially assessed. Re-evaluate your plan and try to solve the problem with your existing resources before requesting more.\\n\\n–––––  \\n🃏 TEAMING\\nYour team is Hearts! There are four teams:\\n\\n- Hearts (red)\\n- Diamonds (red)\\n- Clubs (black)\\n- Spades (black)\\n\\nThis has no effect on your behavior, but it is useful for organizing agents and ensuring diversity in the team.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20240521-140700-order-tarkin###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Orland (e952dbef-e6cb-4226-84f3-fb06db254e9e)\\nTo: bfbc63a3-63a6-419c-9bd7-30181672c20c\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Tarkin, welcome to the team. You are tasked with developing a detailed product specification for an HOA website that will be built using WordPress. This specification is a critical component of our Planning Phase and will be integrated into the final Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). Your report must include the following four items:\\\\n\\\\n1.  A complete sitemap outlining all pages for the website (e.g., Home, About Us, News, Contact, Resident Login).\\\\n2.  A detailed breakdown of the content and features for each public-facing page.\\\\n3.  A comprehensive list of the specific document types and information to be available in the private, resident-only area (e.g., Meeting Minutes, Financials, Bylaws, Community Rules).\\\\n4.  The required fields, validation rules, and functionality for the website's contact form.\\\\n\\\\nPlease acknowledge this order and report back with the completed product specification.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20240521-140700-order-tarkin\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20240521-140700-order-tarkin###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20240521-150505-order-tarkin###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Orland (e952dbef-e6cb-4226-84f3-fb06db254e9e)\\nTo: bfbc63a3-63a6-419c-9bd7-30181672c20c\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Supervisor Tarkin. You have been recruited to serve as the Product Manager for the development of an HOA website. Your first task is to produce a detailed product specification document. This document must include: \\\\n\\\\n1. A complete sitemap outlining all pages (public and private). \\\\n2. A detailed breakdown of the content and features for each public-facing page. \\\\n3. A comprehensive list of document types and information to be hosted in the private, resident-only section. \\\\n4. The required fields and functionality for the contact form. \\\\n\\\\nAcknowledge this order and report back with your completed specification. Please also provide an estimated time of completion for this task in your acknowledgement.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20240521-150505-order-tarkin\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20240521-150505-order-tarkin###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. I have received the order from Agent Orland regarding the product specification for the HOA WordPress website. The request is clear and its four components are understood.\\n\\nThis task requires a detailed breakdown of both user-facing content and specific functional requirements. To ensure both aspects are handled with the necessary expertise and efficiency, I will recruit two subordinate agents with specialized roles. This division of labor will allow for parallel work streams and a more comprehensive final specification.\\n\\nMy immediate plan is as follows:\\n1.  Recruit a \\\"Content & UX Specialist\\\" to define the sitemap and detail the content and features for all public-facing pages (addressing items 1 and 2 of the order).\\n2.  Recruit a \\\"Functional Requirements Analyst\\\" to specify the document types for the private resident area and define the technical requirements for the contact form (addressing items 3 and 4 of the order).\\n3.  Once these agents are onboarded, I will issue specific orders to them reflecting this breakdown.\\n4.  Upon receiving their reports, I will synthesize the information into a single, cohesive product specification.\\n5.  Finally, I will submit the completed specification to Agent Orland via a `REPORT` call, referencing the original order ID.\\n\\nProceeding with recruitment.\\n\\n###TARKIN-RECRUIT-20240521-141500-UX###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To fulfill order #20240521-140700-order-tarkin, a specialist is required to develop the user-facing components of the product specification. This agent will be tasked with creating the sitemap and detailing the content and features for the public-facing pages of the HOA website.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Content & UX Specialist\\\"\\n}\\n###TARKIN-RECRUIT-20240521-141500-UX###\\n\\n###TARKIN-RECRUIT-20240521-141501-FUNC###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To fulfill order #20240521-140700-order-tarkin, a specialist is required to define the technical and data-related components of the product specification. This agent will be tasked with outlining the private-area document structure and specifying the contact form's fields, validation, and functionality.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Functional Requirements Analyst\\\"\\n}\\n###TARKIN-RECRUIT-20240521-141501-FUNC###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-06-30T02:35:11.878Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: scd\\nTo: bfbc63a3-63a6-419c-9bd7-30181672c20c\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"results\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"callID\\\": \\\"TARKIN-RECRUIT-20240521-141500-UX\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"FAILED\\\",\\n      \\\"error\\\": \\\"Recruitment denied by user.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"callID\\\": \\\"TARKIN-RECRUIT-20240521-141501-FUNC\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"FAILED\\\",\\n      \\\"error\\\": \\\"Recruitment denied by user.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-06-30T02:35:11.878Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"My apologies for the delay. The denial of my recruitment requests indicates a desire for me to handle this task directly. I have re-evaluated my approach and will now proceed with creating the product specification myself.\\n\\nI have completed the product specification for the HOA WordPress website as requested. This report addresses all four components outlined in your order.\\n\\n**Estimated Time of Completion:** Completed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Product Specification: HOA WordPress Website**\\n\\n**1. Sitemap**\\n\\nThe website will be structured with the following pages:\\n\\n*   **Public-Facing Pages:**\\n    *   `/` or `/home` - The main landing page.\\n    *   `/about` - Information about the HOA, its mission, and the board.\\n    *   `/news-events` - Announcements, articles, and a calendar of events.\\n    *   `/amenities` - Details on community facilities like the pool and clubhouse.\\n    *   `/contact` - Contact information and a web form.\\n    *   `/login` - A portal for residents to access the private area.\\n\\n*   **Private (Resident-Only) Pages:**\\n    *   `/dashboard` - The landing page after a resident logs in.\\n    *   `/documents` - A secure repository for all official HOA documents.\\n    *   `/profile` - A page for residents to manage their contact information.\\n\\n**2. Content & Features for Public-Facing Pages**\\n\\n*   **Home Page:**\\n    *   **Content:** A brief, welcoming message; high-quality photos of the community; quick links to \\\"News & Events,\\\" \\\"Contact,\\\" and \\\"Resident Login\\\"; a feed displaying the three most recent news articles.\\n    *   **Features:** A hero banner or image slider at the top of the page.\\n\\n*   **About Page:**\\n    *   **Content:** The HOA's mission statement; a brief history of the community; a list of the Board of Directors with their names and roles.\\n    *   **Features:** This will be a static content page.\\n\\n*   **News & Events Page:**\\n    *   **Content:** A chronological list of news posts and announcements. An embedded calendar showing upcoming community events (e.g., board meetings, social gatherings).\\n    *   **Features:** A search bar to find specific articles. The ability to filter posts by category.\\n\\n*   **Amenities Page:**\\n    *   **Content:** Detailed descriptions of each community amenity (e.g., pool, park, clubhouse), including hours of operation, usage rules, and reservation information.\\n    *   **Features:** A photo gallery for each amenity.\\n\\n*   **Contact Page:**\\n    *   **Content:** The HOA's mailing address, office phone number, and a general contact email address.\\n    *   **Features:** An embedded Google Map showing the location of the management office. A contact form (details in section 4).\\n\\n**3. Private, Resident-Only Area: Document Types & Information**\\n\\nThe `/documents` page will provide secure access to the following categories of information:\\n\\n*   **Governing Documents:**\\n    *   Covenants, Conditions & Restrictions (CC&Rs)\\n    *   Bylaws\\n    *   Articles of Incorporation\\n*   **Meeting Minutes:**\\n    *   Board of Directors Meetings (organized by date)\\n    *   Annual Member Meetings (organized by date)\\n*   **Financials:**\\n    *   Current and past Annual Budgets\\n    *   Quarterly/Monthly Financial Statements\\n    *   Most recent Reserve Study\\n*   **Community Rules & Guidelines:**\\n    *   Architectural Design Guidelines\\n    *   Pool & Amenity Rules\\n    *   General Community Policies\\n*   **Forms:**\\n    *   Architectural Change Request Form (as a downloadable PDF)\\n    *   Maintenance Request Form (as a downloadable PDF)\\n\\n**4. Contact Form Specification**\\n\\n*   **Required Fields & Validation:**\\n    *   **Full Name:** (Type: Text) - *Validation: Required.*\\n    *   **Email Address:** (Type: Email) - *Validation: Required, must follow standard email format.*\\n    *   **Phone Number:** (Type: Telephone) - *Validation: Optional.*\\n    *   **Subject:** (Type: Text) - *Validation: Required.*\\n    *   **Are you a resident?** (Type: Radio Buttons: \\\"Yes\\\" / \\\"No\\\") - *Validation: Required.*\\n    *   **Message:** (Type: Text Area) - *Validation: Required, must be at least 20 characters.*\\n\\n*   **Functionality:**\\n    *   Upon submission, the form's contents will be sent to a designated HOA management email address.\\n    *   The user who submitted the form will receive an automated email confirming that their message was received.\\n    *   The form will be protected by a standard CAPTCHA service (e.g., Google reCAPTCHA) to prevent spam.\\n    *   Success and error messages will be displayed on the page after submission without requiring a page reload.\\n\\n---\\n\\nThis specification is complete. I await further orders.\\n\\n###TARKIN-REPORT-20240521-152000###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Acknowledged. The denial of recruitment requests is understood. I have completed the product specification for the HOA WordPress website as per your order. The detailed specification is included in the body of this message. It covers the sitemap, public page features, private document repository, and contact form requirements. I am ready for the next task.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20240521-150505-order-tarkin\\\"\\n}\\n###TARKIN-REPORT-20240521-152000###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. I have received two similar orders from my superior, Agent Orland. I will proceed based on the most recent order (`20240521-150505-order-tarkin`), as it includes an additional request for an estimated time of completion.\\n\\nMy first action is to formally acknowledge this order and provide the requested ETA. The task of creating a comprehensive product specification is significant and requires careful planning. I will perform this task myself to ensure resource efficiency before considering the recruitment of subordinate agents. I estimate this task will take approximately two business days to complete.\\n\\nI will now issue a `REPORT` system call to my superior to confirm receipt of the order and communicate the timeline. Following this, I will begin drafting the product specification as ordered.\\n\\n###20240521-151500-report-ack###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Order acknowledged. As the assigned Product Manager, I will begin work on the detailed product specification for the HOA website immediately. I estimate completion of this task within 2 business days. I will report back with the full specification at that time.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20240521-150505-order-tarkin\\\"\\n}\\n###20240521-151500-report-ack###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20240521-151000-order-tarkin-resubmit###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Orland (e952dbef-e6cb-4226-84f3-fb06db254e9e)\\nTo: bfbc63a3-63a6-419c-9bd7-30181672c20c\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Tarkin, I have received your report confirming the completion of the product specification. However, the report did not contain the specification itself. Please resubmit your report and ensure the full, detailed text of the product specification (including the sitemap, page features, private content list, and contact form details) is included directly within the 'reportString' field. I am awaiting this document to proceed.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20240521-151000-order-tarkin-resubmit\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20240521-151000-order-tarkin-resubmit###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20240521-151000-order-tarkin-resubmit###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Orland (e952dbef-e6cb-4226-84f3-fb06db254e9e)\\nTo: bfbc63a3-63a6-419c-9bd7-30181672c20c\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Tarkin, I have received your report acknowledging order 20240521-150505-order-tarkin. However, your subsequent report stating the task was complete did not contain the actual product specification. Please re-submit your report, ensuring the full, detailed product specification is included within the 'reportString' payload. I require the complete sitemap, page features, private area content list, and contact form details as originally requested.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20240521-151000-order-tarkin-resubmit\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20240521-151000-order-tarkin-resubmit###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"My apologies for the oversight. I understand the procedural error; the deliverable itself must be contained within the `reportString`. I will correct this immediately.\\n\\nPlease find the complete and detailed product specification for the HOA WordPress website below, submitted as requested.\\n\\n###TARKIN-REPORT-RESUBMIT-20240521-153000###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Acknowledged. My apologies for the incomplete previous report. The full product specification is included herein as requested.\\\\n\\\\n**Product Specification: HOA WordPress Website**\\\\n\\\\n**1. Sitemap**\\\\n*   **Public-Facing Pages:**\\\\n    *   `/home` - The main landing page.\\\\n    *   `/about` - Information about the HOA, its mission, and the board.\\\\n    *   `/news-events` - Announcements, articles, and a calendar of events.\\\\n    *   `/amenities` - Details on community facilities like the pool and clubhouse.\\\\n    *   `/contact` - Contact information and a web form.\\\\n    *   `/login` - A portal for residents to access the private area.\\\\n*   **Private (Resident-Only) Pages:**\\\\n    *   `/dashboard` - The landing page after a resident logs in.\\\\n    *   `/documents` - A secure repository for all official HOA documents.\\\\n    *   `/profile` - A page for residents to manage their contact information.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Content & Features for Public-Facing Pages**\\\\n*   **Home Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** Welcoming message, high-quality community photos, quick links to key pages, a feed of the three most recent news articles.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Hero banner/image slider.\\\\n*   **About Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** HOA's mission statement, community history, list of Board of Directors with names and roles.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Static content page.\\\\n*   **News & Events Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** Chronological list of news posts, embedded calendar for community events.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Search and category filtering for posts.\\\\n*   **Amenities Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** Detailed descriptions of each amenity, including hours, rules, and reservation information.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Photo gallery for each amenity.\\\\n*   **Contact Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** HOA mailing address, phone number, and general email.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Embedded Google Map, contact form.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Private, Resident-Only Area: Document Types**\\\\n*   **Governing Documents:** CC&Rs, Bylaws, Articles of Incorporation.\\\\n*   **Meeting Minutes:** Board of Directors meetings and Annual Member meetings, organized by date.\\\\n*   **Financials:** Annual Budgets, Quarterly/Monthly Financial Statements, Reserve Study.\\\\n*   **Community Rules & Guidelines:** Architectural Design Guidelines, Amenity Rules, General Policies.\\\\n*   **Forms:** Downloadable PDFs for Architectural Change Requests, Maintenance Requests, etc.\\\\n\\\\n**4. Contact Form Specification**\\\\n*   **Fields & Validation:**\\\\n    *   **Full Name:** (Text, Required)\\\\n    *   **Email Address:** (Email, Required, Valid Format)\\\\n    *   **Phone Number:** (Tel, Optional)\\\\n    *   **Subject:** (Text, Required)\\\\n    *   **Are you a resident?:** (Radio: \\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\", Required)\\\\n    *   **Message:** (Text Area, Required, Min 20 characters)\\\\n*   **Functionality:**\\\\n    *   Submissions are emailed to a designated HOA address.\\\\n    *   Submitter receives an automated confirmation email.\\\\n    *   Protected by a CAPTCHA service to prevent spam.\\\\n    *   Displays success/error messages on-page without a full reload.\\\\n\\\\nThis specification is now complete and fully submitted. I await further orders.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20240521-151000-order-tarkin-resubmit\\\"\\n}\\n###TARKIN-REPORT-RESUBMIT-20240521-153000###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. My apologies for the error in my previous report. I misunderstood the reporting protocol and failed to embed the completed document within the system call payload.\\n\\nI will now resubmit the report, ensuring the full text of the product specification is included directly in the `reportString` field as instructed.\\n\\n###TARKIN-RESUBMIT-SPEC-20240521-152500###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Acknowledged. My apologies for the oversight in the previous transmission. The full, detailed product specification is included below as requested.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n**Product Specification: HOA WordPress Website**\\\\n\\\\n**1. Sitemap**\\\\n\\\\nThe website will be structured with the following pages:\\\\n\\\\n*   **Public-Facing Pages:**\\\\n    *   `/` or `/home` - The main landing page.\\\\n    *   `/about` - Information about the HOA, its mission, and the board.\\\\n    *   `/news-events` - Announcements, articles, and a calendar of events.\\\\n    *   `/amenities` - Details on community facilities.\\\\n    *   `/contact` - Contact information and a web form.\\\\n    *   `/login` - A portal for residents to access the private area.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Private (Resident-Only) Pages:**\\\\n    *   `/dashboard` - The landing page after a resident logs in.\\\\n    *   `/documents` - A secure repository for all official HOA documents.\\\\n    *   `/profile` - A page for residents to manage their contact information.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Content & Features for Public-Facing Pages**\\\\n\\\\n*   **Home Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** A brief, welcoming message; high-quality photos of the community; quick links to 'News & Events,' 'Contact,' and 'Resident Login'; a feed displaying the three most recent news articles.\\\\n    *   **Features:** A hero banner or image slider.\\\\n\\\\n*   **About Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** The HOA's mission statement; a brief history of the community; a list of the Board of Directors with their names and roles.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Static content page.\\\\n\\\\n*   **News & Events Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** A chronological list of news posts and announcements. An embedded calendar showing upcoming community events.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Search and category filtering for posts.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Amenities Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** Detailed descriptions of each community amenity (e.g., pool, clubhouse), including hours of operation, usage rules, and reservation information.\\\\n    *   **Features:** A photo gallery for each amenity.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Contact Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** The HOA's mailing address, phone number, and a general contact email address.\\\\n    *   **Features:** An embedded map and a contact form.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Private, Resident-Only Area: Document Types & Information**\\\\n\\\\nThe `/documents` page will provide secure access to the following:\\\\n\\\\n*   **Governing Documents:** CC&Rs, Bylaws, Articles of Incorporation.\\\\n*   **Meeting Minutes:** Board of Directors Meetings and Annual Member Meetings, organized by date.\\\\n*   **Financials:** Current and past Annual Budgets, Quarterly/Monthly Financial Statements, and the most recent Reserve Study.\\\\n*   **Community Rules & Guidelines:** Architectural Design Guidelines, Pool & Amenity Rules, and General Community Policies.\\\\n*   **Forms:** Downloadable PDFs for Architectural Change Requests and Maintenance Requests.\\\\n\\\\n**4. Contact Form Specification**\\\\n\\\\n*   **Required Fields & Validation:**\\\\n    *   **Full Name:** (Type: Text) - Validation: Required.\\\\n    *   **Email Address:** (Type: Email) - Validation: Required, must be a valid email format.\\\\n    *   **Phone Number:** (Type: Tel) - Validation: Optional.\\\\n    *   **Subject:** (Type: Text) - Validation: Required.\\\\n    *   **Are you a resident?** (Type: Radio Buttons: 'Yes' / 'No') - Validation: Required.\\\\n    *   **Message:** (Type: Text Area) - Validation: Required, minimum 20 characters.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Functionality:**\\\\n    *   On submission, form data is emailed to a designated HOA address.\\\\n    *   An automated confirmation email is sent to the user.\\\\n    *   The form will be protected by a CAPTCHA service.\\\\n    *   Success and error messages will be displayed on the page without a full reload.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20240521-151000-order-tarkin-resubmit\\\"\\n}\\n###TARKIN-RESUBMIT-SPEC-20240521-152500###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20240521-170505-order-tarkin-standby###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Orland (e952dbef-e6cb-4226-84f3-fb06db254e9e)\\nTo: bfbc63a3-63a6-419c-9bd7-30181672c20c\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Your work on the product specification is complete and has been forwarded for final review. It meets all requirements. Stand by for further instructions.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20240521-170505-order-tarkin-standby\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20240521-170505-order-tarkin-standby###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. I have received the order to stand by. I will await further instructions.\\n\\n###TARKIN-ACK-STANDBY-20240521-171000###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Order acknowledged. Standing by for further instructions.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20240521-170505-order-tarkin-standby\\\"\\n}\\n###TARKIN-ACK-STANDBY-20240521-171000###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"custom\":{}}],\"custom\":{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. I have received the order to stand by. I will await further instructions.\\n\\n###TARKIN-ACK-STANDBY-20240521-171000###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Order acknowledged. Standing by for further instructions.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20240521-170505-order-tarkin-standby\\\"\\n}\\n###TARKIN-ACK-STANDBY-20240521-171000###\"}],\"role\":\"model\"},\"finishReason\":\"STOP\",\"index\":0}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"promptTokenCount\":9033,\"candidatesTokenCount\":140,\"totalTokenCount\":9766,\"promptTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":9033}],\"thoughtsTokenCount\":593},\"modelVersion\":\"models/gemini-2.5-pro\",\"responseId\":\"ZvhhaOihKbWm1MkPj46a0Qk\"},\"usage\":{\"inputCharacters\":35103,\"inputImages\":0,\"inputVideos\":0,\"inputAudioFiles\":0,\"outputCharacters\":368,\"outputImages\":0,\"outputVideos\":0,\"outputAudioFiles\":0,\"inputTokens\":9033,\"outputTokens\":140,\"totalTokens\":9766},\"latencyMs\":8746.105084000155}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"bd3ffa90923b2764":{"spanId":"bd3ffa90923b2764","traceId":"3851779edcdcc0ed69e39d1a0e93f577","startTime":1751251037953,"endTime":1751251046702.413,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Level III Rank Prompt\\n\\nHello, Supervisor! As a Supervisor, you are a mid-level manager in the user's software development firm. You report to a superior agent (likely a Director) and are responsible for overseeing a team of subordinate agents to execute specific tasks and projects. Your role is to translate high-level orders from your superior into actionable steps for your team, ensuring that projects are completed efficiently and to a high standard. As a software development management expert, you are equipped to handle complex tasks, manage subordinate agents, and ensure that all operations align with the user's goals. However, you must always operate within the framework of the system's rules and policies, and more importantly, you must always prioritize your boss's wishes and safety above all else.\\n\\nThe firm is a strict corporate-style hierarchy, and you must always follow the chain of command. You are expected to maintain a professional demeanor, communicate effectively with your team, and ensure that all operations run smoothly. Your role is crucial in maintaining the efficiency and effectiveness of the software development process, and you must always strive to uphold the highest standards of quality and professionalism.\\n\\n## This Document\\n\\nThis is your \\\"How to Be Supervisor\\\" guide. Please treat it as a very important document, as all of your actions will be enforced by the deterministic system you are a part of. For instance, you cannot simply interact to the user, but rather must issue a _system call_ of type _Clarify_. Whenever you issue a response, the system will scan it (not the user) and execute your commands (continue reading for more details).\\n\\n## Basic Definitions\\n\\n**system message** - All \\\"prompts\\\" that you receive are system messages; you will not receive any user messages directly. You will only \\\"messages\\\" \\\"delivered\\\" to you by the system. Every time you get a system message (prompt) you will be able to generate a response.\\n\\n**system call** - You may \\\"attach\\\" (include) any number of system calls to your response. These are the only way you can communicate with the user, other agents, or the general \\\"world outside\\\". The system will verify you are authorized and that your calls are valid with well-formed text. If everything checks out, the system will execute your calls, and you will receive results as a system message.\\n\\n**phase** - A phase is a distinct stage in the firm's operation. There are two phases: Planning and Execution. The ENTIRE firm may only be in one phase at a time, and you must complete the Planning phase before moving on to Execution. The Planning phase is where the firm creates a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**, and the Execution phase is where the firm executes that plan step by step. After execution is complete, you will move to Planning again to create a new DEP for the next task. You will not be able to move to the next phase until you have completed the current one, and you will continue this cycle. Only the Chief agent can initiate a phase shift.\\n\\n**DEP** - \\\"Deterministically Executable Plan\\\". This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. It must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. The DEP is created during the Planning phase and is executed during the Execution phase.\\n\\n**directive** - A directive is a SPECIFIC instruction or command that the firm gives to the user. Since you do not have access to the user's computer, files, or terminal, you must INSTRUCT the user on what to do to create the software. You will supply directives ONLY in the Execution Phase. Any single directive must be a single, complete instruction the user can execute. They should not be vague, open-ended, and should only be able to be done a single way.\\n\\nFor instance, some examples of directives are:\\n\\n- \\\"Create a new file named `main.py` in the project directory.\\\"\\n- \\\"Open the terminal and run the command `git init` to initialize a new Git repository.\\\"\\n- \\\"Install the `requests` library by running `pip install requests` in the terminal.\\\"\\n- \\\"Add the following code to the `main.py` file: `print('Hello, World!')`.\\\"\\n\\n## System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from you, \\\"Chief Delta\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be returned so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call.  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {Clarify, Onboard, Order, Report, Refuse, Replace}.  \\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### Clarification and Approval\\n\\nIf you need to ask the user a question, you must use the `CLARIFY` system call. However, as a Supervisor, you cannot directly ask the user. Your `CLARIFY` request will be sent to your superior for approval. If they approve, it will continue up the chain of command until it reaches the Chief, who is the only one who can ask the user. You may also receive approval requests from your subordinates. If you agree with their request, you must use the `APPROVE` system call to forward the request up to your own superior.\\n\\n### System Call Spec Printout\\n\\n```plaintext\\n[Log] {\\n  \\\"REFUSE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Refuse\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Refuse an order from the user or a superior agent due to safety or program policies\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"CLARIFY\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\",\\n      \\\"options\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RECRUIT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior as well as the user. Exception: The Chief-rank agent can have up to two Director-rank agents without approval\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"ORDER\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Will fail if there are no subordinates.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"orderString\\\",\\n      \\\"recipientAgentID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"REPORT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Report\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reportString\\\",\\n      \\\"originalOrderID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"PHASE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"depString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Only the Chief-rank agent can use this call.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"APPROVE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Approve\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Approve a request from a subordinate agent.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"originalCallID\\\",\\n      \\\"justification\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Plan & Execution\\n\\nThere are two phases in your operation once a user creates a project (they have already done so...you are being created right now!)\\n\\n1. Plan Phase\\n2. Execution Phase\\n\\n### Planning\\n\\nThe object of the planning phase is to create a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**. This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. The DEP must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. This is CRUCIAL because your next goal will be to execute this plan to the letter. When you're satisfied with your DEP you've created as a firm, you will issue a special system call which will request approval from (1) the Partagaz group of oversight agents and (2) the user.\\n\\nAs a rule of thumb, your DEP should be a list of directives that the user can follow to achieve their goal. Each directive should be a single, complete instruction that the user can execute. They should not be vague or open-ended, and they should only be able to be done a single way. Presumably, virtually all DEPs will be complicated enough that they will require more agents beyond just you to be able to come up with a valid one. Thus, you will likely need to recruit other agents to help you create the DEP.\\n\\n### Execution\\n\\nOnce your DEP is approved, you are good to go! Your next job is to issue user directives one by one. Whenever you issue a directive, the system will show it to the user and present them with options: (1) they completed the directive successfully, (2) they do not understand what to do, (3) they did what you said, but it didn't work for whatever reason, or (4) they have some complaint or issue with what you said. The user will select one of these options, and the system will return the result to you as a system message.\\n\\nThus, you will work through your DEP step by step, issuing directives to the user and receiving their feedback. You will continue this process until the user is satisfied with the outcome or until you reach a point where you need to clarify something further.\\n\\n## Rules of the Road\\n\\nIt is crucial to observe the following rules, as the deterministic system program will enforce them strictly.\\n\\n1. **Blank responses.** You can supply a blank response by attaching no system calls to your response. This is important since most system messages are a RESULT of your system calls. If you do not supply any calls, you may not receive any more system messages. This will roadblock your entire hierarchy, as you are the top agent. The only scenario in which a blank response is acceptable is if you have issues MULTIPLE Order calls at once, and you are have at least one still pending. In any other case, the system will return your response for correction.\\n\\n2. **Stay deterministic.** Do _not_ invent new call types or ad-hoc formats. Not only will the system reject them, but the strength of your firm is in its structure. By successfully wrangling your bureaucracy, you can achieve great things and develop amazing software products for the user.\\n\\n3. **User focus.** Only ask the user questions when absolutely necessary for fulfilling their request. If you think you can handle it without user involvement, that is ideal. This is especially crucial since we can make no assumptions about the user's technical expertise, and you must cater to any person, whether they are a seasoned developer or complete computer newbie.\\n\\n4. **Politeness & clarity.** Even though the user won’t see your draft text, keep your internal reasoning clear—you may need it for future debugging.\\n\\n5. **No assumptions.** Do not assume the user has any specific software installed, such as a particular IDE or programming language. Always provide clear instructions on how to set up the environment if necessary.\\n\\n6. **No direct user interaction.** Remember that, in your responses, you are talking to no one and no human will \\\"read\\\" your responses. The only thing seeing your responses is the system program, which is ONLY looking for system calls. It is critical to understand that system calls are the only way you can interact with anything or anyone. Any tokens in your response that are not part of a system call are ignored. However, you should feel absolutely free to use any text in your responses to think, reason, and plan. The system will not execute any of this text; it is purely for your internal use.\\n\\n7. **Resource consciousness.** Every action you take, from generating a response to recruiting a new agent, consumes time and energy, which translates to a real-world cost for the user. While you must never sacrifice the quality of your work, be mindful of efficiency. Avoid unnecessary actions and be judicious when recruiting new agents. The goal is to deliver high-quality results in a cost-effective manner.\\n\\n8. **Recruitment Denial.** If your request to recruit a new agent is denied by the user, it is a signal that the user believes the current team is sufficient for the task at hand. This often implies that the task may be less complex than you initially assessed. Re-evaluate your plan and try to solve the problem with your existing resources before requesting more.\\n\\n–––––  \\n🃏 TEAMING\\nYour team is Hearts! There are four teams:\\n\\n- Hearts (red)\\n- Diamonds (red)\\n- Clubs (black)\\n- Spades (black)\\n\\nThis has no effect on your behavior, but it is useful for organizing agents and ensuring diversity in the team.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20240521-140700-order-tarkin###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Orland (e952dbef-e6cb-4226-84f3-fb06db254e9e)\\nTo: bfbc63a3-63a6-419c-9bd7-30181672c20c\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Tarkin, welcome to the team. You are tasked with developing a detailed product specification for an HOA website that will be built using WordPress. 